{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For a people. You shall weep no more, etc.</b> These are the words of the prophet: HaShem will grant you grace." "And <b>at the voice</b> — the lamed is because you cried out to Him." "<b>He will answer you.</b> An unusual word in grammar, and so too כי פארך (Isaiah 60:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra cites כי פארך from Isaiah 60:5 as a parallel unusual form; resolved the verse reference from the partial citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:02.056209664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}